.TH NEPLANG 1 "October 2026" "NepLang" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
neplang \- run a NepLang program
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B neplang
[\fB\-\-vm\fR | \fB\-\-ir\fR | \fB\-\-emit\-c\fR | \fB\-\-build\fR \fB\-o\fR \fIout\fR]
.I file.np
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B neplang
runs a program written in NepLang, a small programming language whose keywords are
romanized Nepali words mixed with English technical terms.
Source files must end in
.BR .np .
.PP
Each statement goes on its own line, and
.B #
starts a comment.
.SH LANGUAGE
.TP
.B vana(expr)
Print a value.
.TP
.B name = expr
Create or update a variable.
.TP
.B yedi cond { } natara yedi cond { } natara { }
If / else-if / else.
.B natara
must be on the same line as the closing
.BR } .
.TP
.B jabasamma cond { }
While loop.
.TP
.B ko_lagi i in a..b { }
Count
.I i
from
.I a
up to, but not including,
.IR b .
.TP
.B kaam name(a, b) { farkau expr }
Define a function;
.B farkau
returns a value.
.TP
.B ko_lagi x in arr { }
Loop over the items of an array, or the characters of a string.
.TP
.B [1, 2, 3]  a[i]  a[i] = v  lambai(a)
Arrays: literal, indexing from 0, item assignment, length.
.TP
.B \(dqNamaste \(dq + naam
Strings: double-quoted, with escapes
.BR \en ,
.BR \et ,
.B \e\(dq
and
.BR \e\e .
.B +
joins strings (a number on either side is turned into text);
.B s[i]
is the i-th character and
.B lambai(s)
the number of characters. Strings can't be changed in place.
.TP
.B class Name { field = 0 ... kaam method() { } }
Define a class. Create an object with
.BR Name(...) ,
which runs the method
.B banau
(the constructor) if there is one. Use
.B obj.field
and
.BR obj.method(...) .
Inside a method, bare field names refer to the current object, and
.B yo
is the object itself. Fields and methods whose names start with
.B _
are private to the class.
.PP
Values are integers, arrays, strings and objects. Comparisons
.B "== != < <= > >="
work on two numbers or two strings and give 1 or 0. A condition must be a number;
any non-zero value is true.
.SH MODES
With no option the program runs on the tree-walking interpreter. \fB\-\-vm\fR compiles it to bytecode and runs it on the virtual machine.
\fB\-\-ir\fR prints the optimized intermediate representation. \fB\-\-emit\-c\fR prints the generated C source.
\fB\-\-build\fR \fB\-o\fR \fIout\fR produces a native executable using the system C compiler (\fBCC\fR or \fBcc\fR).
Classes are supported by the interpreter only.
.SH MODULES
\fBimport "file.np"\fR or \fBimport name\fR includes another file. Files are searched next to the importing file, then in the directories listed in \fBNEPLANG_PATH\fR.
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
kaam factorial(n) {
    yedi n <= 1 {
        farkau 1
    }
    farkau n * factorial(n \- 1)
}
vana(factorial(6))
.fi
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success; 1 on a syntax or runtime error, which is printed with its file, line and
column.
.SH SEE ALSO
https://github.com/charitraa/Nepa
